<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Allstate upgraded.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Allstate upgraded.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- J.P. Morgan said it upgraded Allstate Corp to buy from market performer after the company reported better-than expected third quarter earnings on Thursday.</p>
<p>-- J.P. Morgan cited management actions to reduce catastrophe risk and improve focus by shedding commercial line business.</p>
<p>-- also cited excellent underwriting results in personal auto, and reduced claims costs and favorable industrywide trends. Personal auto makes up about two-thirds of Allstate's premiums.</p>
<p>-- Set new price target of $63, up from $49, and raised 1997 earnings estimate by $0.04, to $4.89 a share.</p>
</text>
